vents","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kdmccormick/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kdmccormick/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kdmccormick/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kdmccormick","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fccn/openedx-platform/commits/95eea1c79ce4045999aa9f00987561c0d97a94d2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-06-09T18:57:58Z","email":"kyle@axim.org","name":"Kyle McCormick"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-06-09T18:57:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"build: Restore .dockerignore to improve image build and caching (#36878)\n\nedx-platform''s Dockerfile was removed in Jan 2025 because the\ncommunity was not maintaining or using it. The PR that removed it [1]\nalso removed the .dockerfile as an effort to clean up unnecessary\nDocker-related files from the repo.\n\nHowever, the .dockerignore file serves an important purpose for\n*any* Docker image based on edx-platform: it identifies which files\nand paths aren''t relevant for the functioning of the image. For\nexample, Tutor greatly benefited from this file, because by ignoring\nunnecessary files, the build context was shrunk and image cache\nlayers were less likely to be unnecesarily invalidated.\n\nWe restore the .dockerfile as it was previously in Sumac [2], with\nthe addition of /venv, /.venv, and __pycache__, and with the\nremoval of /Dockerfile (as it no longer exists).\n\n[1] https://github.com/openedx/edx-platform/pull/35731\n[2] https://github.com/openedx/edx-platform/blob/open-release/sumac.master/.dockerignore\nBackports: 0b48f2795a21a79faa4509b0b3c5986b807f6089","tree":{"sha":"be3b2a8bb514e13d4c8496974eb4ba0f3b0b1e28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fccn/openedx-platform/git/trees/be3b2a8bb514e13d4c8496974eb4ba0f3b0b1e28"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fccn/openedx-platform/git/commits/95eea1c79ce4045999aa9f00987561c0d97a94d2","verification":{"payload":"tree be3b2a8bb514e13d4c8496974eb4ba0f3b0b1e28\nparent f3aa7bfae9b1953525a7af3fd6d972fabce5f3a6\nauthor Kyle McCormick <kyle@axim.org> 1749495478 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1749495478 -0400\n\nbuild: Restore .dockerignore to improve image build and caching (#36878)\n\nedx-platform''s Dockerfile was removed in Jan 2025 because the\ncommunity was not maintaining or using it. The PR that removed it [1]\nalso removed the .dockerfile as an effort to clean up unnecessary\nDocker-related files from the repo.\n\nHowever, the .dockerignore file serves an important purpose for\n*any* Docker image based on edx-platform: it identifies which files\nand paths aren''t relevant for the functioning of the image. For\nexample, Tutor greatly benefited from this file, because by ignoring\nunnecessary files, the build context was shrunk and image cache\nlayers were less likely to be unnecesarily invalidated.\n\nWe restore the .dockerfile as it was previously in Sumac [2], with\nthe addition of /venv, /.venv, and __pycache__, and with the\nremoval of /Dockerfile (as it no longer exists).\n\n[1] https://github.com/openedx/edx-platform/pull/35731\n[2] https://github.com/openedx/edx-platform/blob/open-release/sumac.master/.dockerignore\nBackports: 0b48f2795a21a79faa4509b0b3c5986b807f6089","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJoRy62CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVtgQAHuUwhEMAeXJ1KmlvJZ/kG35\ncKm/Yc0z9opzAWuOfPqtZcspzmLHJdQ24UIrGYrei1dkCIh37R6GNqCGc30bteHT\nW7UrKg9VaeJmUgsM3LoeYHALcATZPKimaZ9Yi2qDEuNAYs/GAtskSEmxAdRpvKzi\nE7f3kjvwWNtV0qbpGRDbocCIEoRPjmTXE8axbFZ1/d2nAA1vqeaXs1hYextGsR19\n+ZQIoFtuxACnq4SP8eOHfO5wpSNBAytVtM0RSetnV5g4mQz9MYS2MjTIJBHN8UT4\nbmqPHo9pqiidvIpuWlXGvH9QsmNjGjrtsmeTkI0YFg0c4tvPOtoB/lvL4kkA4NDR\nOf/5bfpJMz3xoG0MBEav4a1BMDY8+FLUVdWxgJPVwjk1b7n4lssARCTg23E5BU39\nyVDwrtrjHOaw/6CdUKno++NlEE8d4pFhTxR9Z8frPV8ObDFWBx148wpUSq+drQHH\ndiXqgtoKbQDtUWssWVVxXx5nGvn0egi