l":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryok90/yokota.dev/commits/de28210a3456e73abd19c1318049d82371f82c4a"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryok90/yokota.dev/commit/ccdfb7265bb45659e74d15276e9c893cfa083cf2","sha":"ccdfb7265bb45659e74d15276e9c893cfa083cf2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryok90/yokota.dev/commits/ccdfb7265bb45659e74d15276e9c893cfa083cf2"}],"sha":"aad493b226b4ffc06e4cd20b8f903910848d3c44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryok90/yokota.dev/commits/aad493b226b4ffc06e4cd20b8f903910848d3c44"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53323214?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryok90","id":53323214,"login":"ryok90","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMzIzMjE0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryok90/yokota.dev/commits/ccdfb7265bb45659e74d15276e9c893cfa083cf2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T15:43:16Z","email":"ryok90@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Yokota"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T15:43:16Z","email":"ryok90@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Yokota"},"message":"fix: separate the R and Y in the header wordmark badge\n\nThe badge sets RY in Electrolize at 13.6px inside a rotated 2.5rem square, and\nletter-spacing -0.06em closed the pair until the left arm of the Y touched the\nbowl of the R, the same defect just fixed in the favicon. Dropping the negative\ntracking alone only bought 0.8px, so the badge now carries 0.1em of positive\ntracking with a matching text-indent, which cancels the trailing letter-space\nthat CSS adds after the last glyph and keeps the pair optically centered in the\nsquare. Compared 0, 0.06em, 0.1em, and 0.14em rendered in Chromium at 4x: 0.1em\nis where the counter opens without the pair reading as two loose letters.\n\nAudited the rest of the site for the same problem. The product card monograms,\nZC and AI, carry no negative tracking and already have comfortable spacing. The\nother negative letter-spacing rules are all large display headings, where tight\ntracking is deliberate. The social card carries an RY monogram whose letters are\nalready separated by 3px, so it needs no spacing change.\n\nVerified on the Zephyr preview in Chromium at 1024 and 390 wide: computed\nletter-spacing and text-indent are both 1.36px, the badge is unchanged at\n42.7px square, no horizontal overflow. pnpm check reports zero errors, warnings,\nhints.","tree":{"sha":"c46f5f0ae02562f35fc0b1aa4e1b3f3c7f2e2437","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryok90/yokota.dev/git/trees/c46f5f0ae02562f35fc0b1aa4e1b3f3c7f2e2437"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryok90/yokota.dev/git/commits/ccdfb7265bb45659e74d15276e9c893cfa083cf2","verification":{"payload":"tree c46f5f0ae02562f35fc0b1aa4e1b3f3c7f2e2437\nparent c64f7500aaa4a3613f9dd88bbb16af20df47dbce\nauthor Rodrigo Yokota <ryok90@gmail.com> 1789141396 -0300\ncommitter Rodrigo Yokota <ryok90@gmail.com> 1789141396 -0300\n\nfix: separate the R and Y in the header wordmark badge\n\nThe badge sets RY in Electrolize at 13.6px inside a rotated 2.5rem square, and\nletter-spacing -0.06em closed the pair until the left arm of the Y touched the\nbowl of the R, the same defect just fixed in the favicon. Dropping the negative\ntracking alone only bought 0.8px, so the badge now carries 0.1em of positive\ntracking with a matching text-indent, which cancels the trailing letter-space\nthat CSS adds after the last glyph and keeps the pair optically centered in the\nsquare. Compared 0, 0.06em, 0.1em, and 0.14em rendered in Chromium at 4x: 0.1em\nis where the counter opens without the pair reading as two loose letters.\n\nAudited the rest of the site for the same problem. The product card monograms,\nZC and AI, carry no negative tracking and already have comfortable spacing. The\nother negative letter-spacing rules are all large display headings, where tight\ntracking is deliberate. The social card carries an RY monogram whose letters are\nalready separated by 3px, so it needs no spacing change.\n\nVerified on the Zephyr preview in Chromium at 1024 and 390 wide: computed\nletter-spacing and text-indent are both 1.36px, the badge is unchanged at\n42.7px square, no horizontal overflow. pnpm check reports zero errors, warnings,\nhints.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQJPBAABCAA5FiEEI81kj9URlwdIi5LNRmDOkRPPJsIFAmqkIZQbFIAAAAAABAAO\nbWFudTIsMi41KzEuMTIsMCwzAAoJEEZgzpETzybCv9YP/RQYRarnw5DHZ9VNMztC\nzON5tOnRV/fuOoFHe80blRSVPVEU0XNCT5PzinsS3qmIgKfDqzQzIqWG385n0Ssh\nPiYEnzsdC+pADwlvtu+KFEg7qjFfgLdrxQ523A0gTiO8KatlpsLve50OVPTrN00o\nuUIYJUb47n/KU7tPiMqGvvPsA8cFGJ0gbZ+oX24I9GQ4INbSZVGIK2/9rqXvZalO\nfs+ypLJkXps1k7NY6rCW80RAzUoESVjeCGzcG3UstB0AMcslsxRX8Ej0QKz/VFCH\n/xiXAQWLT0iYioX6XFjmwZdePK4LyEBvaygfiaaR89EhJaAa8wVjijXIZ+PSS6nh\nCW1VnQyRK6jCUPcYm2d0qEZvZjdw0YRdZMPxYf15y7/k3wauJVeDERvAGDcOSpVg\nOlU5eS3cjpCX/r9+NtJGDqcszwx0yXbi2B+4IYei7bsAqKFowDB9EiLJJV1JX8Ek\noqnHHDKsiXyYV68k2NwXT02cs4K3DFsfFs57EhLn53d+NZSTQkMwNTc1YOCNjmAB\nityRjbGKutSQn2ejTxs7H0ADUzvOTNS0MR1QpeZ/aatKgA54GJAicOHffESNidXF\nkkrZc1dJ5zvyQXxrGw0VoQQGtdvZ5OmFXrfJZrxKNW4vIveD+tiBIGzf0mD4LX90\n8YY1lT4PITzYk/AaSABob5vo\n=l6Nm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-11T15:43:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53323214?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryok90","id":53323214,"login":"ryok90","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMzIzMjE0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryok90/yokota.dev/commit/ccdfb7265bb45659e74d15276e9c893cfa083cf2","node_id":"C_kwDOFeKmf9oAKGNjZGZiNzI2NWJiNDU2NTllNzRkMTUyNzZlOWM4OTNjZmEwODNjZjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryok90/yokota.dev/commit/c64f7500aaa4a3613f9dd88bbb16af20df47dbce","sha":"c64f7500aaa4a3613f9dd88bbb16af20df47dbce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryok90/yokota.dev/commits/c64f7500aaa4a3613f9dd88bbb16af20df47dbce"}],"sha":"ccdfb7265bb45659e74d15276e9c893cfa083cf2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryok90/yokota.dev/commits/ccdfb7265bb45659e74d15276e9c893cfa083cf2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53323214?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryok90","id":53323214,"login":"ryok90","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMzIzMjE0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryok90/yokota.dev/commits/c64f7500aaa4a3613f9dd88bbb16af20df47dbce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T15:20:18Z","email":"ryok90@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Yokota"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T15:22:05Z","email":"ryok90@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Yokota"},"message":"fix: open the gap between the R and Y in the monogram\n\nAt font-size 36 with letter-spacing -4 the bowl of the R nearly touched the left\narm of the Y, and at 16px the pair merged into a blob. Dropping the negative\ntracking and taking the type down to 34 restores a real counter between the two\nletters while keeping the monogram''s footprint: the glyphs span 10.5 to 53.9 of\nthe 64 unit canvas against 11.3 to 53.3 before, so the optical size and the\nmargins to the corner brackets are unchanged.\n\nRegenerated every derived icon from the updated SVG, per the rule in AGENTS.md:\n16px, 32px, the 180px Apple touch icon, favicon.ico, and the 192px, 512px, and\n512px maskable manifest icons. The ICO keeps its previous shape, three 32bpp BMP\nentries at 48, 32, and 16, and the file was parsed back and its 32px entry\ndecoded to confirm it is well formed.\n\nVerified on the Zephyr preview: all eight icon URLs return 200 with their\nexpected types, and Chromium''s own render of favicon.svg shows the gap, which\nmatters because browsers rasterize that file themselves rather than using the\nPNGs. pnpm check reports zero errors, warnings, hints.","tree":{"sha":"3e934d794e348b72e88ff1fd8e1bfe5e343314ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryok90/yokota.dev/git/trees/3e934d794e348b72e88ff1fd8e1bfe5e343314ab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryok90/yokota.dev/git/commits/c64f7500aaa4a3613f9dd88bbb16af20df47dbce","verification":{"payload":"tree 3e934d794e348b72e88ff1fd8e1bfe5e343314ab\nparent f61451c1c40c5293414005e69c479716755ca860\nauthor Rodrigo Yokota <ryok90@gmail.com> 1789140018 -0300\ncommitter Rodrigo Yokota <ryok90@gmail.com> 1789140125 -0300\n\nfix: open the gap between the R and Y in the monogram\n\nAt font-size 36 with letter-spacing -4 the bowl of the R nearly touched the left\narm of the Y, and at 16px the pair merged into a blob. Dropping the negative\ntracking and taking the type down to 34 restores a real counter between the two\nletters while keeping the monogram''s footprint: the glyphs span 10.5 to 53.9 of\nthe 64 unit canvas against 11.3 to 53.3 before, so the optical size and the\nmargins to the corner brackets are unchanged.\n\nRegenerated every derived icon from the updated SVG, per the rule in AGENTS.md:\n16px, 32px, the 180px Apple touch icon, favicon.ico, and the 192px, 512px, and\n512px maskable manifest icons. The ICO keeps its previous shape, three 32bpp BMP\nentries at 48, 32, and 16, and the file was parsed back and its 32px entry\ndecoded to confirm it is well formed.\n\nVerified on the Zephyr preview: all eight icon URLs return 200 with their\nexpected types, and Chromium''s own render of favicon.svg shows the gap, which\nmatters because browsers rasterize that file themselves rather than using the\nPNGs. pnpm check reports zero errors, warnings, hints.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQJPBAABCAA5FiEEI81kj9URlwdIi5LNRmDOkRPPJsIFAmqkHJ0bFIAAAAAABAAO\nbWFudTIsMi41KzEuMTIsMCwzAAoJEEZgzpETzybCBk4P/iMOgw4sGQ5MZWuflieC\nFHaRrYHeLTwKu7LkEN96nHqshFqspPOvbhEH8ltsa4A1XFw7PR5+B09pjADZWImO\nDJTOrSFSdZXu7FVoX2RTeej4wBgZdVeaVOhtXuzpW7e+XyK69LCWerHr661IzG/o\nJsu9t6zuiJrO7l29rLnj4VBCIR/PWFva6RHI7N3aa0FIm0FB3rL++2BtO8Ri96yZ\nADneSJqtE/FpO3hUnu/eC/1NhHx/kx0EMPJxhBVo7Dhzx8+wLhtlW5l25vKllHWF\n+ZEdwl1xu1zn