i.github.com/users/ryok90/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryok90/yokota.dev/commits/ad1f5ff6f6b8dcf5bf2414f78c2c317cff973731/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T15:10:08Z","email":"ryok90@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Yokota"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T15:10:08Z","email":"ryok90@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Yokota"},"message":"feat: send unknown paths to the 404 page\n\nZephyr''s static hosting answers unknown paths with the homepage document at\nHTTP 200 instead of 404.html, so /no-such-page rendered the homepage under a\nbogus URL and 404.astro was unreachable in production. A static site cannot\nanswer with a 404 status, so the fix is client side.\n\nLayout.astro emits a routeGuard script into the one document that can be a\nfallback hit: the document built at /. On any other pathname that document is\nbeing served as a catch-all, so the guard calls location.replace(''/404.html'').\nIt is derived from Astro.url.pathname rather than a prop, so it cannot drift,\nand every real route is served from its own file and can never trip it. The\nscript sits directly after <meta charset> and runs before anything paints, so\nthere is no flash of the homepage.\n\nThe status code still comes from the platform and stays 200, which makes this a\nsoft 404. Layout.astro gains a noindex prop and 404.astro passes it, so the\nerror document is not indexable.\n\nVerified on the Zephyr preview in Chromium: / and /links render themselves,\nwhile /no-such-page, /deep/missing/path, and /rodrigo-yokota.vcf/ all land on\n/404.html with \"Signal lost.\" and robots=noindex. The guard is present in\ndist/index.html and absent from dist/links/index.html and dist/404.html, so no\nredirect loop is possible. Renders correctly at 390px. pnpm check reports zero\nerrors, warnings, hints.","tree":{"sha":"b196dd591a523ebe392716b1f1fd73f2cf592ed4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryok90/yokota.dev/git/trees/b196dd591a523ebe392716b1f1fd73f2cf592ed4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryok90/yokota.dev/git/commits/ad1f5ff6f6b8dcf5bf2414f78c2c317cff973731","verification":{"payload":"tree b196dd591a523ebe392716b1f1fd73f2cf592ed4\nparent b16ca22f4421fff60e1889f8337a4030578ac73d\nauthor Rodrigo Yokota <ryok90@gmail.com> 1789139408 -0300\ncommitter Rodrigo Yokota <ryok90@gmail.com> 1789139408 -0300\n\nfeat: send unknown paths to the 404 page\n\nZephyr''s static hosting answers unknown paths with the homepage document at\nHTTP 200 instead of 404.html, so /no-such-page rendered the homepage under a\nbogus URL and 404.astro was unreachable in production. A static site cannot\nanswer with a 404 status, so the fix is client side.\n\nLayout.astro emits a routeGuard script into the one document that can be a\nfallback hit: the document built at /. On any other pathname that document is\nbeing served as a catch-all, so the guard calls location.replace(''/404.html'').\nIt is derived from Astro.url.pathname rather than a prop, so it cannot drift,\nand every real route is served from its own file and can never trip it. The\nscript sits directly after <meta charset> and runs before anything paints, so\nthere is no flash of the homepage.\n\nThe status code still comes from the platform and stays 200, which makes this a\nsoft 404. Layout.astro gains a noindex prop and 404.astro passes it, so the\nerror document is not indexable.\n\nVerified on the Zephyr preview in Chromium: / and /links render themselves,\nwhile /no-such-page, /deep/missing/path, and /rodrigo-yokota.vcf/ all land on\n/404.html with \"Signal lost.\" and robots=noindex. The guard is present in\ndist/index.html and absent from dist/links/index.html and dist/404.html, so no\nredirect loop is possible. Renders correctly at 390px. pnpm check reports zero\nerrors, warnings, hints.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQJPBAABCAA5FiEEI81kj9URlwdIi5LNRmDOkRPPJsIFAmqkGdAbFIAAAAAABAAO\nbWFudTIsMi41KzEuMTIsMCwzAAoJEEZgzpETzybCekUP/R1Ff1FJ0Iva3zPN4dA7\n94UmOU8eL6dkv7jDsuU/xWCrsViWwjCg3n3ZNq/CMZ4Qo1FxS4NkgIQeyrgDdKUQ\nbMIo0A6bstXaDrFegTApt82Jiyei9ncrve7Kc+7Q+LaCMRlgb7wBhnuLxmlUvlbD\nMS793calCjPk1COyKlhipc3/nI6AaONzGSnjuZZMJShRvSDwDt/g8GFy58LUimES\nwSRpGGnz1OvNTxONuN4CMQZX1e2DkZ+Qw6UDokTa+8ozcB/qSXjFvSJRx6qiOwss\npK60GHsg7yFndTqOUE9a/wRDSwEWrQ3Q8lnokrHoZ9JldAtJw4r7Eaxh5Pelb0uE\nDh1G9P6cv+Iew3DatL/+cUNofelPDUeXRYc4P97vTEn3McEwbiR/3XBE7ccX5Abx\nr5kL6RydTRlQ37B0zNYpphYkcDI/EQNO0lbgKukRS7o/SOJukLOv8rTsLJwFR2DS\nH1/rP5aEl/vOYZH1Q2izKdVVk4Brxvt6yH0qIGoYXG2n3217auZOmQkOKo4lFyQB\n1Vq/CzNramxbgudHOGlm53ogtQOpMcoMUYmZ1kksaARRl+DlWLetH3bS5dz/ZIRZ\nNBBMq2CgOCvg+GNfp8LDPHxmrAR9sLTCg4gIYUJbcwZZvCeDqM10Hw8+ny8zlJFg\n1namfSsWsIg4TDP9rjt4GvAC\n=45JB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-11T15:10:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53323214?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryok90","id":53323214,"login":"ryok90","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMzIzMjE0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryok90/yokota.dev/commit/ad1f5ff6f6b8dcf5bf2414f78c2c317cff973731","node_id":"C_kwDOFeKmf9oAKGFkMWY1ZmY2ZjZiOGRjZjViZjI0MTRmNzhjMmMzMTdjZmY5NzM3MzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryok90/yokota.dev/commit/b16ca22f4421fff60e1889f8337a4030578ac73d","sha":"b16ca22f4421fff60e1889f8337a4030578ac73d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryok90/yokota.dev/commits/b16ca22f4421fff60e1889f8337a4030578ac73d"}],"sha":"ad1f5ff6f6b8dcf5bf2414f78c2c317cff973731","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryok90/yokota.dev/commits/ad1f5ff6f6b8dcf5bf2414f78c2c317cff973731"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53323214?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryok90","id":53323214,"login":"ryok90","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMzIzMjE0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryok90","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryok90/yokota.dev/commits/b16ca22f4421fff60e1889f8337a4030578ac73d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T15:32:28Z","email":"ryok90@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Yokota"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T15:32:28Z","email":"ryok90@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Yokota"},"message":"feat: restore install metadata and legacy URLs lost in the Astro migration\n\nAudited the Next to Astro rebuild against the pre-Astro head and against live\nproduction. Three things the migration dropped are worth having back.\n\nWeb app manifest: the old site linked /site.webmanifest with 192px and 512px\nAndroid icons, and the rebuild deleted both. Production answered 404 for the\nmanifest, so an Android home-screen install fell back to the 32px favicon. The\nmanifest is regenerated from favicon.svg, now in the site''s own colors instead\nof the old white theme, and it gains a maskable 512px variant that renders the\nartwork at 410px centered on #090b0d so the corner brackets survive the\ncircular crop. There is no service worker and no offline behavior; this exists\nfor icons and theme color only.\n\n/sitemap.xml: the old site published its sitemap there and @astrojs/sitemap\nowns /sitemap-index.xml, so the previously submitted path returned 404. A\nhand-written index at that path keeps it resolving. It points at sitemap-0.xml\nbecause a sitemap index may not reference another index.\n\n/api/contact: this was the vCard download link on the old links page. Zephyr''s\nHTML fallback answered it with the homepage at HTTP 200, which is worse than a\n404 because it looks like it worked. It now redirects to /rodrigo-yokota.vcf\nthrough a static stub. The redirects config cannot be used here: with\ntrailingSlash always, Astro rewrites the destination to /rodrigo-yokota.vcf/,\nand Zephyr answers that with the homepage.\n\nDeliberately not done. The wot-verification meta tag is gone and stays gone\nunless the MyWOT listing is still wanted. Facebook, Instagram, and YouTube were\ndropped from sameAs and from the links page, which matches the platform\nengineering positioning of the rebuild. /images/rodrigo-yokota.webp, the old\nog:image, stays 404 since social scrapers refresh their caches. The vCard is\nserved as application/octet-stream because static prerendering discards the\ntext/vcard header set in the route; that needs a MIME mapping on the host.\n\nVerified on the Zephyr preview: /site.webmanifest 200 application/manifest+json\nwith all three icons 200, /sitemap.xml 200 application/xml, /api/contact and\n/api/contact/ 200 with the stub, homepage loads with zero console messages and\nthe manifest link resolving. pnpm check reports zero errors, warnings, hints.","tree":{"sha":"4f9ba0d1c88d293ca54ad4bf38a8367d3edd366e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryok90/yokota.dev/git/trees/4f9ba0d1c88d293ca54ad4bf38a8367d3edd366e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryok90/yokota.dev/git/commits/b16ca22f4421fff60e1889f8337a4030578ac73d","verification":{"payload":"tree 4f9ba0d1c88d293ca54ad4bf38a8367d3edd366e\nparent de28210a3456e73abd19c1318049d82371f82c4a\nauthor Rodrigo Yokota <ryok90@gmail.com> 1789054348 -0300\ncommitter Rodrigo Yokota <ryok90@gmail.com> 1789054348 -0300\n\nfeat: restore install metadata and legacy URLs lost in the Astro migration\n\nAudited the Next to Astro rebuild against the pre-Astro head and against live\nproduction. Three things the migration dropped are worth having back.\n\nWeb app manifest: the old site linked /site.webmanifest with 192px and 512px\nAndroid icons, and the rebuild deleted both. Production answered 404 for the\nmanifest, so an Android home-screen install fell back to the 32px favicon. The\nmanifest is regenerated from favicon.svg, now in the site''s own colors instead\nof the old white theme, and it gains a maskable 512px variant that renders the\nartwork at 410px centered on #090b0d so the corner brackets survive the\ncircular crop. There is no service worker and no offline behavior; this exists\nfor icons and theme color only.\n\n/sitemap.xml: the old site published its sitemap there and @astrojs/sitemap\nowns /sitemap-index.xml, so the previously submitted path returned 404. A\nhand-written index at that path keeps it resolving. It points at sitemap-0.xml\nbecause a sitemap index may not reference another index.\n\n/api/contact: this was the vCard download link on the old links page. Zephyr''s\nHTML fallback answered it with the homepage at HTTP 200, which is worse than a\n404 because it looks like it worked. It now redirects to /rodrigo-yokota.vcf\nthrough a static stub. The redirects config cannot be used here: with\ntrailingSlash always, Astro rewrites the destination to /rodrigo-yokota.vcf/,\nand Zephyr answers that with the homepage.\n\nDeliberately not done. The wot-verification meta tag is gone and stays gone\nunless the MyWOT listing is still wanted. Facebook, Instagram, and YouTube were\ndropped from sameAs and from the links page, which matches the platform\nengineering positioning of the rebuild. /images/rodrigo-yokota.webp, the old\nog:image, stays 404 since social scrapers refresh their caches. The vCard is\nserved as application/octet-stream because static prerendering discards the\ntext/vcard header set in the route; that needs a MIME mapping on the host.\n\nVerified on the Zephyr preview: /site.webmanifest 200 application/manifest+json\nwith all three icons 200, /sitemap.xml 200 application/xml, /api/contact and\n/api/contact/ 200 with the stub, homepage loads with zero console messages and\nthe manifest link resolving. pnpm check reports zero errors, warnings, hints.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQJPBAABCAA5FiEEI81kj9URlwdIi5LNRmDOkRPPJsIFAmqizYwbFIAAAAAABAAO\nbWFudTIsMi41KzEuMTIsMCwzAAoJEEZgzpETzybCgKMP/R9Y4trP1Y80bjr4ufnm\ncNkfhZi1eUiYi2P7K9pI+DZCeDCUk/dHiv9KYRELbhFaGkMsrlrViSErOyCgRDXb\niekzE/qikg588LlRWkiXs6R4sG6GBE0+5b4AGmGcJs4AHHPxGMGb7l2r05UNU6EB\nW6ZYMECpu5Qh4BR4E9fa83MokXCgUi83xPctjek0DdZNCSmFA7lYLh9rfSfCiyxo\n2qy0EbEBAsEJef+Ldo2CXZcA983uPSH3sJjfUFj7Wwwob8NqTzfovXGqgwnTPp2m\nEpBccHaAmNwdXBqEqz9CW397oEThQRxhqR6Fb2I6hVOcovvYWoro0diBPhwlU8ST\nzRtFkUwoQS1u7RJ4zr3U8X4GPNlRqXSnN03oK5Zz2RR5pnPTFP2ZxHmxmq4pARbs\n7THpww8Ajfmzj1BNxCdzmuD9n9bUxdEcLK4/pbIEvmKaomJhu2QLrXydjkh7eXy+\nUDLOyRg4pMz1FrxSF+vWAKZKQ7/z3mT3ZO6SOkrpyuWWl+7paHb3N5uym2d2YbQy\n3z2sD316sdvXD1OKc8xoGY0FwMbylQuTYLXI7t98JdiZmiBqR2D+LmQjul+ius