onical domain\n\nReinstate GA4 property G-EYT1QRFKV1, dropped when the portfolio moved to\nAstro, as an is:inline script in the shared layout so Astro never bundles\nit and dist keeps emitting zero JavaScript assets.\n\nTraffic separation has to happen at runtime. Every build renders canonical\nyokota.dev URLs and Zephyr previews are production builds, so neither the\nmarkup nor import.meta.env.PROD distinguishes them. Zephyr''s edge domain is\nze.yokota.dev and version URLs are single-label subdomains of the apex, so a\nsuffix test would match every version URL; the guard is an exact apex\nhostname match, recorded as such in the code comment and AGENTS.md.\n\nRefs #3","tree":{"sha":"c60da638c527d1fb7af217a37c07680f2d143c2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryok90/yokota.dev/git/trees/c60da638c527d1fb7af217a37c07680f2d143c2a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryok90/yokota.dev/git/commits/5919615c9f6a5bfbcfc98cee774390548a297a6f","verification":{"payload":"tree c60da638c527d1fb7af217a37c07680f2d143c2a\nparent de08203447996883ec3ce97dbe6eda9c763e322d\nauthor Rodrigo Yokota <ryok90@gmail.com> 1789049195 -0300\ncommitter Rodrigo Yokota <ryok90@gmail.com> 1789049195 -0300\n\nfeat: restore Google Analytics tag on the canonical domain\n\nReinstate GA4 property G-EYT1QRFKV1, dropped when the portfolio moved to\nAstro, as an is:inline script in the shared layout so Astro never bundles\nit and dist keeps emitting zero JavaScript assets.\n\nTraffic separation has to happen at runtime. Every build renders canonical\nyokota.dev URLs and Zephyr previews are production builds, so neither the\nmarkup nor import.meta.env.PROD distinguishes them. Zephyr''s edge domain is\nze.yokota.dev and version URLs are single-label subdomains of the apex, so a\nsuffix test would match every version URL; the guard is an exact apex\nhostname match, recorded as such in the code comment and AGENTS.md.\n\nRefs #3\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQJPBAABCAA5FiEE