:{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34070216?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NethmiRodrigo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NethmiRodrigo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NethmiRodrigo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NethmiRodrigo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NethmiRodrigo","id":34070216,"login":"NethmiRodrigo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MDcwMjE2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NethmiRodrigo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NethmiRodrigo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NethmiRodrigo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NethmiRodrigo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NethmiRodrigo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NethmiRodrigo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management/commits/7dc40adfde68677979aa9422d5d00858a8213121/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T15:24:37Z","email":"nethmi@openmrs.org","name":"Nethmi Rodrigo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T15:24:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(fix) O3-5983: Add the actions menu back to in-service patient cards (#2752)\n\n* (fix) O3-5983: Add the actions menu back to in-service patient cards\n\nThe in-service cards on the queue page replaced the table rows that carried\nthe Move, Edit, Remove patient and Undo transition actions, so those actions\nwere lost.\n\nEach card now has an overflow menu in its top-right corner with those four\nactions, reusing the queue table''s action menu items so the handlers, labels\nand visibility rules stay in one place. The menu sits outside the patient\nchart link so opening it does not navigate away.\n\n* (fix) O3-5983: Render queue actions as direct menu items and move the card menu beside the link\n\nCarbon''s OverflowMenu clones each direct child with the ref and focus handlers its keyboard navigation relies on. The shared wrapper component dropped them, so arrow keys did not move between items in the card menu or the queue table. Replace the wrapper with a hook that returns the visible OverflowMenuItems directly.\n\nMark the shared remove action as a delete action to match its danger confirmation button.\n\nPlace the card''s actions menu beside the patient chart link instead of over it, so the two hit areas do not overlap. The service row extends under the menu column so its divider still reaches the card edge.\n\n* (fix) O3-5983: Move the card actions menu into the queue status bar, outside the patient chart link","tree":{"sha":"6d569b46d850ef2b0814c529132fecfa1fb814b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management/git/trees/6d569b46d850ef2b0814c529132fecfa1fb814b2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management/git/commits/7dc40adfde68677979aa9422d5d00858a8213121","verification":{"payload":"tree 6d569b46d850ef2b0814c529132fecfa1fb814b2\nparent 71b3d3f10534189eafd4786628aeceecdb4a84c2\nauthor Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org> 1790090677 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790090677 +0530\n\n(fix) O3-5983: Add the actions menu back to in-service patient cards (#2752)\n\n* (fix) O3-5983: Add the actions menu back to in-service patient cards\n\nThe in-service cards on the queue page replaced the table rows that carried\nthe Move, Edit, Remove patient and Undo transition actions, so those actions\nwere lost.\n\nEach card now has an overflow menu in its top-right corner with those four\nactions, reusing the queue table''s action menu items so the handlers, labels\nand visibility rules stay in one place. The menu sits outside the patient\nchart link so opening it does not navigate away.\n\n* (fix) O3-5983: Render queue actions as direct menu items and move the card menu beside the link\n\nCarbon''s OverflowMenu clones each direct child with the ref and focus handlers its keyboard navigation relies on. The shared wrapper component dropped them, so arrow keys did not move between items in the card menu or the queue table. Replace the wrapper with a hook that returns the visible OverflowMenuItems directly.\n\nMark the shared remove action as a delete action to match its danger confirmation button.\n\nPlace the card''s actions menu beside the patient chart link instead of over it, so the two hit areas do not overlap. The service row extends under the menu column so its divider still reaches the card edge.\n\n* (fix) O3-5983: Move the card actions menu into the queue status bar, outside the patient chart link","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsp21CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARmQQAAoplMkUAykN/vEw5a+tnRON\nOJansm/HalwNHRgXoTywRlVQ4KwRzLQ3hWCzACRRFFtToXmPmZMCkv8twm0qPisS\nEeGqlcz7SzzlXj+xej9Qf/0TElk8bOnEFouAChW75Sl/qJdtISaEQbpo/A2tFEHp\nzluNp++YYkNfLeYwkMwn0lGgTt05CRw3iiJ1GWzwdVlthNGC7weqbuNQDjliB3sA\nlm3fjDzFsHGLSmWMRLDi3lkF5XklqwYlaYxH7fkdR2sMW9tskFXclTLSS4YrN8+F\nr35pp3ZZf2y+P61BHFpwq01082UIfeXJQaO6HD4TCBap8ZN+Rp3X3rcsbPfAYyim\nA1lbLhP1BHzyDREO/F/GfnflcdJM1SrN60XfwO0NKq8ko5mA/fhr2r61UHeqAHp/\nZ2FLrjn0YTbY6yLxaINbFZJ5dFjJfK149a9gfofZy4rjyYOGZ0dX/STimSGfbzBb\nLDFxJrNxkMekYPqcF76Cf/9hLx4tHd0z7IyjJx8/aVrbXSKvOLWxFsAj+L7s437Q\niHpjkLlkiFQUP3cdDyeG55kETfox6T11vJND3iiiEfo0YHucArMWFmYtxlhubW01\nHzlsk2EpcN91PPiSAKEJapFl4djzZv7tKkEHUc75HiXkN6ty4yAX+/+5bzPmXzo1\nD+cCQiVcr9bQ1pmqL+gT\n=T19g\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T15:24:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url