405"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1236702?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/claude","id":209825114,"login":"claude[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDODIGtWg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management/commits/f84ddd07fecbfb7a99ee72dbe95493aed423f128/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T15:08:17Z","email":"209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"claude[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T15:08:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(fix) Don''t crash the registration form when address hierarchy levels aren''t JSON (#2756)\n\nThe addresshierarchy module''s `getOrderedAddressHierarchyLevels.form` endpoint\ncontent-negotiates: with a browser-style `Accept` header it can answer with a\n200 response carrying an OpenMRS HTML page instead of the expected JSON array.\n`openmrsFetch` parses the body in a try / catch, so that response resolves as a\nsuccess with `data` left `undefined`, and no error is set.\n\n`useOrderedAddressHierarchyLevels` then derived `orderedFields` with no\nfallback, so `AddressComponent` ran `orderedFields.map(...)` on `undefined` and\nthrew during render, white-screening the whole registration form.\n\nGive the derived arrays a fallback and validate the response body in a shared\nfetcher, so a body that isn''t the expected array is reported through SWR''s\n`error` instead of masquerading as an empty result. The address field\ncomponent''s existing `errorFetchingFieldOrder` guard then renders its error\nnotification rather than an address section with no fields.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AikhgxvEhGWfpnA7NXedfZ\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4f5f19645b36277a7d1e4a02b2e926556fbcf3d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management/git/trees/4f5f19645b36277a7d1e4a02b2e926556fbcf3d6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management/git/commits/f84ddd07fecbfb7a99ee72dbe95493aed423f128","verification":{"payload":"tree 4f5f19645b36277a7d1e4a02b2e926556fbcf3d6\nparent 4f6944cc87106a2c5a59558189084d1dde29c2f2\nauthor claude[bot] <209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1789744097 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789744097 -0700\n\n(fix) Don''t crash the registration form when address hierarchy levels aren''t JSON (#2756)\n\nThe addresshierarchy module''s `getOrderedAddressHierarchyLevels.form` endpoint\ncontent-negotiates: with a browser-style `Accept` header it can answer with a\n200 response carrying an OpenMRS HTML page instead of the expected JSON array.\n`openmrsFetch` parses the body in a try / catch, so that response resolves as a\nsuccess with `data` left `undefined`, and no error is set.\n\n`useOrderedAddressHierarchyLevels` then derived `orderedFields` with no\nfallback, so `AddressComponent` ran `orderedFields.map(...)` on `undefined` and\nthrew during render, white-screening the whole registration form.\n\nGive the derived arrays a fallback and validate the response body in a shared\nfetcher, so a body that isn''t the expected array is reported through SWR''s\n`error` instead of masquerading as an empty result. The address field\ncomponent''s existing `errorFetchingFieldOrder` guard then renders its error\nnotification rather than an address section with no fields.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AikhgxvEhGWfpnA7NXedfZ\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrVPhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7YsQABtPWy+imMJC5wXAt5MbttAa\ncxdif6OxDYTCwVgS64NtzBEtwsTWvvUFYUujXAeQL6AUq4Tt3u6GQPPHeYedHebZ\nr7BgSNn9hIkvZtTDW91mqqgHs9RYfSO5RTUQxtIDmmEyIaU7ggDRgpaY6xR/vxQw\n0sR+sGKvvQ2mvj3DFW5CTbDFoM6kZ1nF93FDeQILycBesrAJpQiuwLfjPwVYgaZw\nbSsBBfI1NB3Q5iB34gFoOxOnbwJLBfs+BsGn99nUIXwPUXv2E5EquAR3mFYPU3J9\nkwPQQ7LJSEWuCqOB9y0tvLF7XzfzcOSkH29FMCLRbC8GGr5yAUcwOYVu5q+W/Ye2\n1hmi7hbVI+4W4Fw8hrYhrvZF4wUkgDKGrpAs+DrIdu2IY5nq3ajxeH8Fi7B7w2ta\n8HX3SF7SMTkzramRSrssowXFW54cEL06sOE6WyZx4Ki9RXy51zPzJMoVfQec6w3o\nqptSMAlTmmLrrPYbwYePWXeJN5X29kfMaCyr72cLCTh7dTf2I10o93pQxsh0G2MO\ngvRokoQjkilKWxffBWzTx9OHbi1PbBLkfeLcEyBS7ZqoL+zsV/BXUSX51k2v53XM\noy5kwpiyuc2MBnIAwwtRbEg5pDqOMIL41zQQJyiIaMSqN3VgOEJBbD6D10umPxFx\nGAC0w1ve1Wx7rv/id0fS\n=dnWF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T15:08:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starre