22cef9a774fd836cb8fa622"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8509731?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/denniskigen","id":8509731,"login":"denniskigen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MDk3MzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management/commits/dab9f79eef9f57aeee91bd237c0d6431cd9c4f43/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T17:50:28Z","email":"kigen.work@gmail.com","name":"Dennis Kigen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T17:50:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(fix) Tell the user when the refine filters, not the query, emptied the search results (#2725)\n\n* (fix) Tell the user when the refine filters, not the query, emptied the search results\n\nWhen a refine filter matched nothing, the results area showed the same message as a query with no hits, \"Sorry, no patient charts were found\" with a hint to retry with the patient''s ID. That points the user at the wrong fix. When the query found patients and the filters removed all of them, the empty state now reads \"No patients match these filters\" with a hint to remove or change a filter, following the filter empty states in the queues, active visits, patient lists and ward apps. A query that itself found nothing keeps the original message.\n\n* Keep loading until every page has landed before blaming the filters\n\nThe filters run over the rows loaded so far, and a broad search arrives in waves. After page 1 lands, isLoading is false while later pages are still in flight, so a filter that only matches a later page showed \"No patients match these filters\" until that page arrived. The results now stay in the loading state while the filtered set is empty and pages are still arriving, and the message appears only once loading has settled. Between waves isValidating drops for a render before the next wave is requested, so the check also compares the pages needed with the pages requested.\n\n* docs: clarify translated empty-state props\n\nDocument that the empty-state title and hint expect already translated strings, and describe their default messages.","tree":{"sha":"775f41104ffe56376e182ce72410585b71df9e4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management/git/trees/775f41104ffe56376e182ce72410585b71df9e4e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management/git/commits/dab9f79eef9f57aeee91bd237c0d6431cd9c4f43","verification":{"payload":"tree 775f41104ffe56376e182ce72410585b71df9e4e\nparent d544f28a430707feba18e7f8b22f2c1b106577e5\nauthor Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com> 1789062628 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789062628 +0000\n\n(fix) Tell the user when the refine filters, not the query, emptied the search results (#2725)\n\n* (fix) Tell the user when the refine filters, not the query, emptied the search results\n\nWhen a refine filter matched nothing, the results area showed the same message as a query with no hits, \"Sorry, no patient charts were found\" with a hint to retry with the patient''s ID. That points the user at the wrong fix. When the query found patients and the filters removed all of them, the empty state now reads \"No patients match these filters\" with a hint to remove or change a filter, following the filter empty states in the queues, active visits, patient lists and ward apps. A query that itself found nothing keeps the original message.\n\n* Keep loading until every page has landed before blaming the filters\n\nThe filters run over the rows loaded so far, and a broad search arrives in waves. After page 1 lands, isLoading is false while later pages are still in flight, so a filter that only matches a later page showed \"No patients match these filters\" until that page arrived. The results now stay in the loading state while the filtered set is empty and pages are still arriving, and the message appears only once loading has settled. Between waves isValidating drops for a render before the next wave is requested, so the check also compares the pages needed with the pages requested.\n\n* docs: clarify translated empty-state props\n\nDocument that the empty-state title and hint expect already translated strings, and describe their default messages.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqou3kCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAu2EQADCa+UUaYB/2Fd7KImxP/EdT\nXClbH37TvDsC5QvASLtz3fN3XUQNq6FJUQFh9caNS7JJF6DYTOyqxrxaNhrHTPuV\nm2iRamadQniowAeHEIpLe8LrH2hjF8JgyXmXWzhywU4QnLaYxuQWeRV+fdZWueFV\nrWuPz/kh2OzQHigAs5FwnHABDoCAy0PN6dszaOm/QkGM4MgH68WlkGWIpLgI3Q6n\ndorGAjCQAsR9nM12/1/SXXMzhRdH0e8td2ytdEwHDAppffa0kKVN3oBnP0QFHJuf\nV45LC1tmSqwaHf9/W4Kw9GjsC3L7fvu7h3zhO8yqvt3N0+vp6f+Bgnygo9s0b5f3\nmz4womHH29SgsszF+f0jxl5RpcVL/TBbpwroZYa3fDeqFwCEPZ4S/qA3UwtkvFGR\nKbRR6mNgV31ZpX2kifshHyS1lhEoVGOxWXZz4ka2r7geMtLX8xDFQeApOMiaLa/j\nFkgG8m+DbKohvDk4DnTPBBZGEjdzqj5I6XmeQbeIDdNiUduMergRLH19zdOzCREr\npmqUPm+fX5btm5bYyq7oXtETI+MeH1a2rEupYgDiQdq4AwrHh4MyB50ow8hDA46t\nv2/WP1i59zF/bE4GoevBZ67yju0GvrhmX2ZLHBnYuM6JztOiBY66FvCKX5TJ30nH\n3nYwUYHQ00ga1Ut25fxM\n=RKGT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-10T17:50:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"http