hub.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management/commits/fcb7a36a901fe4e7072a88dd88e6b6dd1ea72627"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177609628?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UjjawalPrabhat/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UjjawalPrabhat/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UjjawalPrabhat/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UjjawalPrabhat/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/UjjawalPrabhat","id":177609628,"login":"UjjawalPrabhat","node_id":"U_kgDOCpYbnA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UjjawalPrabhat/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UjjawalPrabhat/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UjjawalPrabhat/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UjjawalPrabhat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UjjawalPrabhat/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/UjjawalPrabhat","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management/commits/b8335ad593a4946dd297a88e00c1fd6e6d1fc4f0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T12:40:11Z","email":"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com","name":"Ujjawal Prabhat"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T12:40:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(fix) O3-5940: Don''t offer queues a patient is already in (#2710)\n\n* (fix) O3-5940: Don''t offer queues a patient is already in\n\n* (fix) O3-5940: Don''t submit a prefilled service before the entries load\n\nA service prefilled from the dashboard was submittable while the lookup of the\npatient''s queue entries was still in flight: the queues had loaded, so the\npriority defaulted and the form was valid behind the Service skeleton, and a\nquick submit posted a queue entry that the filter would have excluded a moment\nlater. The priority default now waits for those entries, so submitting during\nthat window fails validation instead of reaching the server.\n\n* (fix) O3-5940: Let the Service field carry the queue filtering on its own\n\nFiltering whole locations out of the Location dropdown required a second,\nunscoped useQueues() call just to group queues by location, plus a reset\neffect to clear a location that disappeared underneath the user. Drop both\nand filter only the Service options, which already load scoped to the\nselected location. When the patient is in every queue there, the select\nrenders empty with helper text saying so, and the required error is\nsuppressed so it does not replace that text on blur. The misconfiguration\nnotice now keys off the unfiltered queue list, and the priority skeleton\nwaits on the queue entries alongside the services.\n\nDuplicate submissions come back as a generic \"Invalid Submission\" message\nwith the identifying code in globalErrors, so getErrorMessage appends those\ncodes and the queue fields reuse isDuplicateQueueEntryError instead of\nmatching the message alone.\n\n* (fix) O3-5940: Address review feedback on duplicate detection and the Service field\n\nRead the duplicate error code from `globalErrors`, where the backend actually\nreports it, and keep `getErrorMessage` free of it so the code no longer leaks\ninto the snackbar subtitle two modals build from it. Let a genuine validation\nerror still surface on the Service field, with the \"already in every queue\"\nmessage carried as its error text rather than suppressing `invalid`.\n\nAlso make `patientUuid` optional, since every caller passes a value that may be\nundefined, and drop the `memoizedQueueLocations` memo: `useFhirFetchAll` returns\na fresh array on every render, so its dependency never matched and the memo\nnever once returned a cached value.\n\n* Fix duplicate-queue error messages and prefilled service edge case\n\n- Read globalErrors from the backend response so validation errors like\n  \"already in this queue\" surface instead of a generic message.\n- Clear a prefilled service selection once queue entries confirm the\n  patient is already enrolled in it.\n\n* (fix) O3-5940: Warn when the active queue entry lookup fails\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\nCo-authored-by: NethmiRodrigo <nethmi.dilinika@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"2f02cfb01d6976fe9b29966f3dc4cc64d5affd86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management/git/trees/2f02cfb01d6976fe9b29966f3dc4cc64d5affd86"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management/git/commits/b8335ad593a4946dd297a88e00c1fd6e6d1fc4f0","verification":{"payload":"tree 2f02cfb01d6976fe9b29966f3dc4cc64d5affd86\nparent 18fbddf63da0df9b17e6f9c7daca6aa0a728e0e1\nauthor Ujjawal Prabhat <UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com> 1788871211 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788871211 +0000\n\n(fix) O3-5940: Don''t offer queues a patient is already in (#2710)\n\n* (fix) O3-5940: Don''t offer queues a patient is already in\n\n* (fix) O3-5940: Don''t submit a prefilled service before the entries load\n\nA service prefilled from the dashboard was submittable while the lookup of the\npatient''s queue entries was still in flight: the queues had loaded, so the\npriority defaulted and the form was valid behind the Service skeleton, and a\nquick submit posted a queue entry that the filter would have excluded a moment\nlater. The priority default now waits for those entries, so submitting during\nthat window fails validation instead of reaching the server.\n\n* (fix) O3-5940: Let the Service field carry the queue filtering on its own\n\nFiltering whole locations out of the Location dropdown required a second,\nunscoped useQueues() call just to group queues by location, plus a reset\neffect to clear a location that disappeared underneath the user. Drop both\nand filter only the Service options, which already load scoped to the\nselected location. When the patient is in every queue there, the select\nrenders empty with helper text saying so, and the required error is\nsuppressed so it does not replace that text on blur. The misconfiguration\nnotice now keys off the unfiltered queue list, and the priority skeleton\nwaits on the queue entries alongside the services.\n\nDuplicate submissions come back as a generic \"Invalid Submission\" message\nwith the identifying code in globalErrors, so getErrorMessage appends those\ncodes and the queue fields reuse isDuplicateQueueEntryError instead of\nmatching the message alone.\n\n* (fix) O3-5940: Address review feedback on duplicate detection and the Service field\n\nRead the duplicate error code from `globalErrors`, where the backend actually\nreports it, and keep `getErrorMessage` free of it so the code no longer leaks\ninto the snackbar subtitle two modals build from it. Let a genuine validation\nerror still surface on the Service field, with the \"already in every queue\"\nmessage carried as its error text rather than suppressing `invalid`.\n\nAlso make `patientUuid` optional, since every caller passes a value that may be\nundefined, and drop the `memoizedQueueLocations` memo: `useFhirFetchAll` returns\na fresh array on every render, so its dependency never matched and the memo\nnever once returned a cached value.\n\n* Fix duplicate-queue error messages and prefilled service edge case\n\n- Read globalErrors from the backend response so validation errors like\n  \"already in this queue\" surface instead of a generic message.\n- Clear a prefilled service selection once queue entries confirm the\n  patient is already enrolled in it.\n\n* (fix) O3-5940: Warn when the active queue entry lookup fails\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\nCo-authored-by: NethmiRodrigo <nethmi.dilinika@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoAIrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkWoQAH30TYcMOosw4l6snAm/A6bO\nohm0YtCvzkvGMiYZRh94b4AyB/4cbVUFoHL85G2ZFz4f6h7jmp8FrHsQiyyil/eI\nS/y4vMbzOgfXsUprGyMWQOOgp8KE3s2arD+VMXd7N4IOpxuigshrTbvn1XK0OQbf\nv88jC3M3gOz9j/ewCz2yd7ssrtNzF0zXU3w/pDHAUwD+MpjtnjaDNve1AY1JI+7h\nwtgI0vA6pX4HmO5TjnJwbOUlINQDw0QVOwN8X8mhgSNBjuoyc91yK+uJEgM9v0FT\nxKjK5SmLT4y+6EFiXUXSzk8/YNRD5DqePUf7FVv36F2p1g4fIUywHkbwKta/BhFP\nEdYHlWNwZVoWaoY9k68bDUia7knn19bixhErt13GL7vTqhW+Cd5X21CXrk54zCfk\n5r8TFlDhrn+UeydNNQT2+ZOOEQU97lAKTqD9UuZ6KuNrZiYDmz6SDd6xIIq9TA+E\naka8lKivO+vZzSINm+BK6+EtiA+sFYFOB7u5uFr4pSyvaORL8bmkKAossjd8+DSa\n2cM6MjQLOv/WJo9iD0825o4eOk2Ady28kNF/aUsJyijMMSXGrYnMK7X7wro4A7vQ\n25bMB449Vcb+rk04YpOSNrsMV0Baz2xQDCzxqIz0yOcso1MW0CLhqTg/oA6InZck\n+W4hHKyLzbwTymVkZSYZ\n=9shN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T12:40:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management/commit/b8335ad593a4946dd297a88e00c1fd6e6d1fc4f0","node_id":"C_kwDOFfdDqNoAKGI4MzM1YWQ1OTNhNDk0NmRkMjk3YTg4ZTAwYzFmZDZlNmQxZmM0ZjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-pat